WEBVTT

00:05.005 --> 00:06.047
This is pissing me off.

00:06.131 --> 00:08.425
Just come out now
if you're going to switch places.

00:12.429 --> 00:14.139
What's wrong, brat?

00:36.453 --> 00:39.748
The Innate Domain is sealed, and
the Special Grade Cursed Spirit is dead.

00:42.000 --> 00:44.294
What's left is
for Itadori to return safely…

00:47.797 --> 00:51.593
Sorry, but he's not coming back.

00:53.386 --> 00:54.804
Don't be so scared.

00:54.888 --> 00:58.433
I'm in a good mood right now,
so let's chat.

01:01.352 --> 01:05.440
This must be the price he's paying
for using me without any restraint.

01:05.523 --> 01:08.443
He seems to be having
some trouble switching back.

01:09.819 --> 01:11.696
But, well…

01:11.780 --> 01:13.656
It is only a matter of time.

01:17.452 --> 01:18.870
So…

01:18.953 --> 01:21.623
I thought about what I could do now.

01:30.340 --> 01:31.758
What are you…

01:38.848 --> 01:41.267
I'm going to take him hostage.

01:41.351 --> 01:42.602
Hostage?

01:42.685 --> 01:46.022
That's right.
I can still live without this,

01:46.105 --> 01:47.690
but not the brat.

01:49.359 --> 01:51.986
If he switches with me, he'll die.

01:52.695 --> 01:54.072
And also…

01:55.490 --> 01:57.200
I'm doing this to make doubly sure.

01:59.953 --> 02:01.746
Sukuna's finger.

02:01.830 --> 02:04.958
That Special Grade Cursed Spirit inside
must have had it.

02:06.501 --> 02:10.130
Okay, I'm finally free.

02:10.213 --> 02:13.216
You can start to panic,
I'm going to kill you.

02:13.967 --> 02:15.635
There's no reason.

02:18.096 --> 02:21.432
Our roles have reversed,
compared to that time.

03:58.947 --> 04:02.575
Only the inequality of reality
can equally exist.

04:15.755 --> 04:17.340
You don't seem to understand.

04:17.423 --> 04:18.925
That guy…

04:19.008 --> 04:21.177
Itadori will be back.

04:21.261 --> 04:23.888
Even at the cost of his life.

04:23.972 --> 04:25.682
That's how he is.

04:25.765 --> 04:27.392
You're flattering him too much.

04:27.475 --> 04:31.521
He's just a moron
who's a little stronger than most people.

04:32.605 --> 04:37.110
He was trembling
with the fear of dying earlier…

04:37.193 --> 04:40.446
while talking pretentiously to himself.

04:41.739 --> 04:42.949
I'm sure that

04:43.032 --> 04:45.535
he doesn't have
the guts to commit suicide.

04:46.536 --> 04:48.454
His hand has regenerated.

04:55.670 --> 04:58.881
He can use the Reverse Cursed Technique.

05:00.091 --> 05:01.884
Sukuna has completely possessed him.

05:01.968 --> 05:05.471
Even if he can live without a heart,
he should be able to receive damage.

05:06.556 --> 05:09.559
I have to restore Itadori's heart
before he comes back.

05:09.642 --> 05:13.187
I have to convince him that he won't win
with a body that doesn't have a heart.

05:15.023 --> 05:17.025
Can I do that?

05:18.526 --> 05:21.571
I couldn't even move
in front of a Special Grade Cursed Spirit.

05:26.034 --> 05:28.202
It's not a matter
of whether I can do it or not.

05:28.286 --> 05:29.704
I have to do it!

05:35.168 --> 05:37.336
I finally managed to come out.

05:37.420 --> 05:39.047
Let's make full use of this place!

05:47.180 --> 05:48.473
How interesting.

05:48.556 --> 05:53.269
You're using a Shikigami,
so why would you come at me personally?

06:00.151 --> 06:01.402
More!

06:02.320 --> 06:03.654
More.

06:05.156 --> 06:07.283
More!

06:09.827 --> 06:11.954
Put more curse into it…

06:13.790 --> 06:15.124
and come at me.

06:19.128 --> 06:20.004
Great Serpent!

06:26.344 --> 06:27.720
All together now!

06:39.315 --> 06:41.776
See? I told you.

06:42.860 --> 06:44.987
Let's make full use of this place!

07:08.928 --> 07:11.264
He's not even casting sorcery.

07:11.347 --> 07:15.476
His strength and agility
are on a totally different level!

07:15.560 --> 07:17.353
Nice technique!

07:29.115 --> 07:30.199
What should I do?

07:30.950 --> 07:35.163
I used Shikigami once
to leave the Innate Domain.

07:36.414 --> 07:39.667
White Divine Dog
and Great Serpent were destroyed.

07:40.168 --> 07:43.296
On top of that, Nue is at its limit.

07:44.422 --> 07:47.133
It's better to dispel it
before it's destroyed.

07:51.012 --> 07:52.054
I see.

07:52.138 --> 07:56.434
So you use shadows
as a medium for your Shikigami?

07:56.517 --> 07:59.353
It doesn't matter if he finds out now.

08:00.104 --> 08:01.481
So what?

08:02.732 --> 08:05.985
It's not a common curse technique
that uses charms,

08:06.068 --> 08:07.945
so it can be used in a lot of situations.

08:08.654 --> 08:11.949
I don't understand. Back then…

08:12.033 --> 08:13.910
Why did you escape?

08:16.954 --> 08:19.165
It's a waste of your talent.

08:20.291 --> 08:21.626
Forget it.

08:22.460 --> 08:25.755
In any case, I won't heal myself
with an attack like that.

08:25.838 --> 08:27.715
He's seen through me.

08:27.798 --> 08:30.301
You're risking your life
over such a foolish motive.

08:30.384 --> 08:33.554
This brat doesn't even deserve it.

08:36.349 --> 08:39.060
Then why did you save me?

08:42.355 --> 08:47.527
Only the inequality of reality
can equally exist.

08:50.738 --> 08:52.907
If I have the ability to curse someone,

08:52.990 --> 08:55.660
I would rather think about those
who are dear to me.

08:56.953 --> 08:59.497
She's indisputably kind.

09:01.791 --> 09:04.585
She deserved to have a happy life
more than anyone else.

09:05.628 --> 09:08.172
Despite so, Tsumiki was cursed.

09:11.384 --> 09:15.513
My father, who named me "Megumi"
even though he didn't know my gender,

09:16.097 --> 09:18.975
is still living his life
brazenly somewhere.

09:23.354 --> 09:26.107
Karma is not something
that happens automatically.

09:27.942 --> 09:31.237
Evil people can only
be punished under the law.

09:33.864 --> 09:37.577
Jujutsu Sorcerers act
as one of the gears in karma.

09:42.540 --> 09:47.086
To ensure more good people
can enjoy equality…

09:51.340 --> 09:56.470
I will save people unfairly.

10:00.725 --> 10:01.976
Brilliant.

10:02.476 --> 10:03.853
This is brilliant.

10:03.936 --> 10:08.357
So you're just getting fired up.

10:08.441 --> 10:10.026
I see.

10:10.109 --> 10:11.694
Well…

10:11.777 --> 10:12.987
In that case,

10:13.904 --> 10:16.782
show me what you're made of,
Megumi Fushiguro!

10:19.994 --> 10:24.373
Furube, yurayura.

10:30.588 --> 10:32.256
Just to make it clear…

10:33.716 --> 10:38.971
I didn't have a logical reason
to save you back then.

10:39.055 --> 10:43.643
Even if it's dangerous, I didn't want
to see a good person like you die.

10:44.143 --> 10:49.899
I had my doubts, but I eventually
heeded my selfish emotions.

10:50.983 --> 10:52.902
But that's all right.

10:53.694 --> 10:55.655
I'm no hero.

10:58.074 --> 10:59.533
I'm a Jujutsu Sorcerer.

11:00.951 --> 11:06.123
So I've never regretted saving you.

11:11.337 --> 11:12.963
Is that so?

11:13.047 --> 11:15.925
You are really smart, Fushiguro.

11:16.008 --> 11:18.135
You probably think way more than I do.

11:18.719 --> 11:21.180
I think that what you believe in is right,

11:21.263 --> 11:23.724
but I don't think I'm wrong either.

11:27.561 --> 11:28.687
Oh, man.

11:28.771 --> 11:30.773
Sorry, but it's almost time.

11:30.856 --> 11:34.068
You, Kugisaki, and Mr. Gojo…

11:34.151 --> 11:36.654
I guess I don't need
to worry about you guys.

11:38.447 --> 11:40.825
Live a long life, you hear me?

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.203
Hey, what's going on?

00:12:31.287 --> 00:12:36.917
Was it really necessary
to lose a valuable finger

00:12:37.001 --> 00:12:38.836
just to confirm Sukuna's strength?

00:12:39.336 --> 00:12:43.549
Well, we won't get anywhere
with a half-hearted test.

00:12:44.133 --> 00:12:45.968
We did gain something from that.

00:12:46.051 --> 00:12:48.888
I hope you're not making excuses.

00:12:52.057 --> 00:12:55.561
Shut up! I can't understand a single word.

00:12:58.147 --> 00:13:01.192
I can't understand it, but the words
speak directly into my brain.

00:13:01.275 --> 00:13:02.735
It's so gross!

00:13:05.112 --> 00:13:07.323
CAFE RESTAURANT RISE

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.658
Welcome!

00:13:09.742 --> 00:13:12.369
Table for one, sir?

00:13:13.996 --> 00:13:15.915
Yes, one.

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.803
I told them to choose
between escape and death

00:13:29.887 --> 00:13:31.597
when they encounter an enemy.

00:13:32.264 --> 00:13:36.560
I've made sure to tell them not to fight.

00:13:38.395 --> 00:13:39.688
That was intentional, right?

00:13:39.772 --> 00:13:40.648
What?

00:13:40.731 --> 00:13:42.441
What do you mean by that?

00:13:42.525 --> 00:13:44.485
They were up against
a Special Grade Curse,

00:13:44.568 --> 00:13:46.904
and had to rescue
five people with unclear status.

00:13:46.987 --> 00:13:49.532
There's no way they would get
the first-years to do this.

00:13:50.366 --> 00:13:54.036
And I was the one who forcibly granted

00:13:54.119 --> 00:13:56.455
an indefinite postponement
on Yuji's death sentence.

00:13:56.539 --> 00:13:58.415
The higher-ups were unhappy,

00:13:58.499 --> 00:14:00.834
so they used a Special Grade Curse
while I was away…

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:04.463
to get rid of him silently.

00:14:05.548 --> 00:14:09.009
Even if the other two died,
it would have served to spite me.

00:14:09.093 --> 00:14:11.387
That's killing two birds
with one stone, isn't it?

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:13.472
No, but…

00:14:13.556 --> 00:14:15.724
When I sent them over,
I really didn't expect it

00:14:15.808 --> 00:14:18.018
to turn into
a Special Grade Cursed Spirit.

00:14:18.519 --> 00:14:20.604
It's troublesome
to find the one behind this.

00:14:21.772 --> 00:14:24.233
Let's just…

00:14:25.317 --> 00:14:27.736
kill all the higher-ups, shall we?

00:14:31.198 --> 00:14:33.450
It's rare to see you get so emotional.

00:14:34.243 --> 00:14:36.453
Good work today, Ms. Ieiri!

00:14:36.954 --> 00:14:40.708
You really like him.

00:14:42.167 --> 00:14:45.504
I'm a nice guy
who's always thinking about the students.

00:14:46.005 --> 00:14:48.299
Don't bully Ijichi too much.

00:14:48.966 --> 00:14:51.719
It's not easy for him to get caught
between us and the chief.

00:14:51.802 --> 00:14:53.345
-Speak more…
-I'm not interested

00:14:53.429 --> 00:14:55.556
-Speak more!
-in a man's pain and suffering.

00:14:55.639 --> 00:14:56.765
Is that so?

00:14:57.516 --> 00:14:59.018
So is he the one?

00:15:01.478 --> 00:15:03.480
Sukuna's vessel.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:06.942
I'm free to tear him apart, right?

00:15:07.568 --> 00:15:09.403
Make good use of him.

00:15:09.486 --> 00:15:10.905
Oh, I will.

00:15:11.906 --> 00:15:13.407
Who do you think I am?

00:15:18.537 --> 00:15:20.706
"Live long," he says?

00:15:21.874 --> 00:15:24.418
How can he say that when he's dead?

00:15:25.336 --> 00:15:28.088
Is this your first time
experiencing a friend's death?

00:15:28.756 --> 00:15:30.549
It's a first for my classmate.

00:15:31.258 --> 00:15:32.843
I see.

00:15:32.927 --> 00:15:34.845
Yet you look surprisingly calm.

00:15:35.387 --> 00:15:36.513
You too.

00:15:36.597 --> 00:15:40.184
Of course.
I've only known him for two weeks.

00:15:40.768 --> 00:15:46.690
I'm not so weak that
I'll cry over a man's death.

00:15:48.651 --> 00:15:49.944
Darn it.

00:16:01.288 --> 00:16:02.539
It's so hot.

00:16:05.167 --> 00:16:08.212
You're right. I wonder when we'll get
to wear our summer uniforms.

00:16:16.762 --> 00:16:18.514
What's going on?

00:16:19.264 --> 00:16:22.977
Your face looks even worse
than usual, Megumi!

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.645
Are you mourning?

00:16:25.771 --> 00:16:27.189
Zenin.

00:16:27.272 --> 00:16:30.192
-Don't call me by my last name!
-Maki!

00:16:30.275 --> 00:16:31.819
I'm talking here!

00:16:31.902 --> 00:16:34.822
Don't you know why they look so depressed?

00:16:34.905 --> 00:16:36.198
What do you mean?

00:16:36.782 --> 00:16:38.492
Someone really died yesterday!

00:16:38.575 --> 00:16:40.703
It was one of the first-year boys!

00:16:40.786 --> 00:16:41.704
Bonito flakes.

00:16:42.788 --> 00:16:44.707
Say it earlier!

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:48.043
That would make me
a heartless witch, wouldn't it?

00:16:48.127 --> 00:16:49.461
But that's who you are!

00:16:49.545 --> 00:16:50.713
Tuna mayonnaise.

00:16:50.796 --> 00:16:53.757
-You're wrong! I can be considerate, okay?
-Who are they?

00:16:54.258 --> 00:16:55.801
They are the second-year students.

00:16:56.343 --> 00:16:59.471
Be gentle with your juniors.

00:16:59.555 --> 00:17:02.307
How is pampering considered being gentle?

00:17:02.391 --> 00:17:06.353
Zenin is the best student
when it comes to using Cursed Tools.

00:17:06.437 --> 00:17:07.730
Salted salmon roe.

00:17:07.813 --> 00:17:09.732
This is Inumaki, a Cursed Speech Sorcerer.

00:17:09.815 --> 00:17:12.359
His vocabulary is limited
to onigiri filling ingredients.

00:17:12.443 --> 00:17:16.280
But you're gentler when you're with Yuta.

00:17:16.363 --> 00:17:17.364
This is Panda.

00:17:18.198 --> 00:17:21.201
We still have one more senior, Okkotsu.

00:17:21.285 --> 00:17:24.204
He's the only one I respect, but…

00:17:25.998 --> 00:17:27.166
He's currently overseas.

00:17:27.249 --> 00:17:29.877
So you're just going to say
that's Panda, and nothing else?

00:17:30.961 --> 00:17:33.172
My apologies.

00:17:33.255 --> 00:17:35.090
Sorry to disturb your mourning.

00:17:35.174 --> 00:17:37.301
Please forgive us!

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.679
Actually, we hoped
that you two will attend

00:17:40.763 --> 00:17:42.765
the Kyoto Sister-School Goodwill Event.

00:17:43.265 --> 00:17:46.101
Kyoto Sister-School Goodwill Event?

00:17:47.019 --> 00:17:48.187
What's that?

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:51.774
It's an exchange
with another sorcery school in Kyoto.

00:17:52.691 --> 00:17:55.903
But isn't that for
second and third-year students?

00:17:56.487 --> 00:17:59.323
Those good-for-nothing third-years
are suspended from school.

00:17:59.406 --> 00:18:00.949
So you guys have to come.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:05.120
So what's the exchange for?
Playing Super Smash Bros?

00:18:05.204 --> 00:18:07.372
I won't lose
if they're playing the Wii version.

00:18:07.456 --> 00:18:09.249
I'll trash them with my Meteor Smash.

00:18:09.333 --> 00:18:11.293
Then three of us will play together.

00:18:12.086 --> 00:18:16.006
In the goodwill event, the principals
of the Tokyo and Kyoto High School

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:19.510
will propose their own methods of dueling.

00:18:19.593 --> 00:18:22.513
Each method takes one day,
so that's two days in total.

00:18:23.097 --> 00:18:24.890
And that's the official consensus.

00:18:24.973 --> 00:18:28.477
We have group battles on the first day,
and individual battles on the second.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:29.853
It's always been like this.

00:18:29.937 --> 00:18:31.105
Salmon.

00:18:31.605 --> 00:18:34.149
Group battles and individual battles?

00:18:35.359 --> 00:18:37.736
So Jujutsu Sorcerers
are going to fight one another?

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:42.866
Yes. It's a sorcery battle
without any rules, except you can't kill.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:46.829
In order not to get killed,
we'll provide intensive training.

00:18:48.956 --> 00:18:52.376
Wait, do you guys actually
have time for this?

00:18:52.459 --> 00:18:54.878
I thought Jujutsu Sorcerers
are always understaffed.

00:18:54.962 --> 00:18:59.049
That's a good question.
The answer is yes, for now.

00:18:59.133 --> 00:19:02.261
Human depression often accumulates
from late winter to early spring,

00:19:02.344 --> 00:19:05.472
and then erupts in early summer,
which in turn transforms into curses.

00:19:05.556 --> 00:19:07.099
That's when we're the busiest.

00:19:07.182 --> 00:19:09.560
We're mostly busy all year long,

00:19:09.643 --> 00:19:11.937
but things should be settling down soon.

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:13.230
I see.

00:19:13.313 --> 00:19:14.898
So you guys are coming, right?

00:19:14.982 --> 00:19:17.067
Your classmate's dead, after all.

00:19:17.151 --> 00:19:18.527
-I'll do it!
-I'll do it!

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:19.528
I…

00:19:19.611 --> 00:19:20.988
I…

00:19:21.655 --> 00:19:25.200
I want to be strong,
and I'll do anything for it.

00:19:26.535 --> 00:19:29.454
But if the training and the games
turn out to be meaningless,

00:19:29.538 --> 00:19:30.664
I'm leaving immediately.

00:19:30.747 --> 00:19:31.832
Me too.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:36.503
That's the arrogant spirit we need.

00:19:36.587 --> 00:19:37.796
Bonito flakes.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:40.215
CAFE RESTAURANT RISE

00:19:40.299 --> 00:19:42.551
That means, your boss…

00:19:42.634 --> 00:19:46.555
wants to subvert the position
of humans and curses.

00:19:47.139 --> 00:19:48.765
Am I right?

00:19:48.849 --> 00:19:51.143
Well, you got the gist of it.

00:19:51.226 --> 00:19:53.312
But there's something different.

00:19:53.812 --> 00:19:56.231
Humans are full of lies.

00:19:56.315 --> 00:19:58.609
Beneath the emotions
and actions they show,

00:19:58.692 --> 00:20:00.903
there's always something hidden in them.

00:20:02.029 --> 00:20:06.200
But negative emotions
like hate and murder…

00:20:06.283 --> 00:20:08.619
They are the irrefutable truth.

00:20:09.119 --> 00:20:12.456
We, the curses born
from these negative emotions,

00:20:12.539 --> 00:20:15.792
are the only real, pure humans!

00:20:15.876 --> 00:20:18.128
The fake ones should just disappear.

00:20:18.212 --> 00:20:22.257
And yet, you guys
are being wiped out right now.

00:20:22.341 --> 00:20:25.052
That's why I'm here to ask you…

00:20:25.135 --> 00:20:27.930
How can we win
against the Jujutsu Sorcerers?

00:20:28.513 --> 00:20:30.098
Before the war begins,

00:20:30.641 --> 00:20:33.477
you need to fulfill two conditions
in order to beat them.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.604
What are the two conditions?

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:40.108
First, the one known
as the strongest Jujutsu Sorcerer…

00:20:40.692 --> 00:20:43.779
We must ensure that Satoru Gojo
is unable to fight.

00:20:44.404 --> 00:20:45.447
Secondly,

00:20:45.948 --> 00:20:50.118
you have to make Ryomen Sukuna
and Yuji Itadori your ally.

00:20:51.453 --> 00:20:57.125
Wait. Isn't that Yuji Itadori brat dead?

00:20:57.918 --> 00:20:58.877
I wonder…

00:20:59.461 --> 00:21:00.837
Who knows?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.971
Don't look up without my permission.

00:21:09.054 --> 00:21:10.180
It makes me sick…

00:21:10.764 --> 00:21:12.224
Brat.

00:22:46.443 --> 00:22:48.403
-Juju Stroll!
-Salmon.

00:22:49.237 --> 00:22:50.280
It stinks.

00:22:50.781 --> 00:22:52.574
It doesn't stink.

00:22:53.283 --> 00:22:54.409
It stinks.

00:22:54.493 --> 00:22:56.411
It doesn't stink!

00:22:56.495 --> 00:23:00.999
Why are you treating me like an animal?

00:23:01.083 --> 00:23:02.417
It's because you're a panda.

00:23:02.501 --> 00:23:03.710
Mustard.

00:23:03.794 --> 00:23:05.462
It smells like a wild animal.

00:23:05.545 --> 00:23:08.173
I asked it to take a bath, but it refused.

00:23:08.256 --> 00:23:10.509
I don't want to get wet.

00:23:10.592 --> 00:23:13.845
But I don't sweat, unlike you guys.

00:23:13.929 --> 00:23:16.181
And I use deodorant every day.

00:23:16.765 --> 00:23:19.392
So I don't stink.

00:23:24.272 --> 00:23:27.776
And that's what happened.
Come over and take a sniff.

00:23:28.276 --> 00:23:32.155
-Sniff…
-Sniff…

00:23:32.239 --> 00:23:35.867
-Sniff…
-Sniff…

00:23:37.452 --> 00:23:41.039
It doesn't stink,
but it smells like the sun.

00:23:42.499 --> 00:23:45.085
-The sun?
-The sun?
